 are scattered on a memorial ground).\n* **Cost:** Communal cremation is generally inexpensive; private cremation costs more. Call your vet’s office to ask about pricing and drop-off procedures.\n\n### 4. Municipal / Waste Disposal (If Other Options Aren't Feasible)\nIf burial or cremation isn't possible, some local municipalities allow small pets to be placed with household waste, but regulations vary strictly by region.\n* If this is your only option, double-bag the remains securely in plastic.\n* Alternatively, many local animal shelters or animal control departments accept deceased small pets for free or a low-cost sanitary disposal.\n\n---\n\n**In the meantime:**\nIf you need a few hours or a couple of days to make arrangements, wrap your hamster gently in a towel or tissue paper, place it inside a sealed plastic bag or container, and store it in a cool place (a cold garage, refrigerator, or freezer) to prevent decomposition.",
