            "text": "To eliminate an enemy player in *Call of Duty*, you need to deplete their health (and armor, if playing a mode like *Warzone*) to zero. Here are the primary ways to do it:\n\n### 1. Weapon Combat (Guns)\n* **Shoot:** Aim at the enemy and fire. \n  * **Aim Down Sights (ADS):** Always aim using your weapon's sights (L2/LT on controller, Right-Click on mouse) for better accuracy, rather than hip-firing, unless they are extremely close.\n  * **Headshots:** Aim for the upper chest and head. Headshots deal significantly more damage and will take enemies down much faster (lowering your \"Time to Kill\" or TTK).\n\n### 2. Melee Attacks\n* If you are right next to an enemy, use the melee button (usually clicking the Right Stick on controller, or 'E' / 'V' on PC) to hit them with your weapon or a knife. \n* Most standard multiplayer modes require two melee hits to kill, but hitting them from behind or using dedicated melee weapons (like combat knives) can eliminate them in one hit.\n\n### 3. Lethal Equipment\n* Use grenades, Semtex, C4, Proximity Mines, or Throwing Knives (R1/RB on controller, Middle-Click or 'G' on PC) to damage or instantly eliminate enemies, especially those hiding behind cover.\n\n### 4. Executions (Finishing Moves)\n* If you sneak directly behind an enemy unnoticed, **press and hold** the melee button. This triggers a cinematic takedown animation that instantly kills the player, regardless of their health or armor.\n\n### 5. Killstreaks / Scorestreaks\n* Earning a streak of kills or points allows you to call in offensive support, such as Cruise Missiles, Precision Airstrikes, Mortar Strikes, or Chopper Gunners, which can eliminate multiple enemies at once.\n\n### Key Tips for Winning Gunfights:\n* **Use Cover:** Never stand completely out in the open. Shoot from behind walls, crates, or low cover (using the \"Mount\" mechanic can also reduce weapon recoil).\n* **Watch the Mini-Map:** Look for red dots, which indicate unsilenced enemy gunfire, or red pings from a friendly UAV.\n* **Control Recoil:** Pull slightly down on your aim stick or mouse while firing in full-auto to keep your shots on target.",
